E2O₂ = I2O₁ - I2O₂

where I2O₁ is the induced energy of the reactants and I2O₂ is the induced energy of the products.

The reaction is:

[E(H₂O)6]₂³ + 2K₂ = [E(Cl4)2]₂³

The given values are:

- The free energy of formation for [Fe(Cl4)2]₂³ = -392 kJ/mol
- The free energy of hydration for E2⁺ = -340 kcal/mol
- The free energy of hydrogen for Cl₂ = -381 kcal/mol

The standard hardness of the reaction is:

