E2O₂ = (E2O₂ + 2H2O) - (E2Cl42 + 2H2O)

E2O₂ = (0 + 2(-340 kcal/mol)) - (-392 kJ/mol + 2(-381 kJ/mol))

E2O₂ = -680 kcal/mol + 392 kJ/mol + 762 kJ/mol

E2O₂ = 484 kJ/mol

The standard halfensity change for the reaction is $\boxed{484}$ kJ/m.
