\]
We can separate the limit into two parts:
\[
\lim_{t \to \infty} \left( \frac{1}{3} \sin t + \cos t \right) e^{-t/2} + \lim_{t \to \infty} 4
\]
The limit of the constant term is:
\[
\lim_{t \to \infty} 4 = 4
\]
For the other term, we have:
\[
\lim_{t \to \infty} \left( \frac{1}{3} \sin t + \cos t \right) e^{-t/2}
\]
