To calculate the acceleration of the particle, we can use the formula of motion:

Force (F) = mass (m) x acceleration (v)

Rearranging to solve for acceleration:

Acceleration (v) = Force (F) / mass (m)

Plugging in the given values:

Acceleration (v) = 32 N / 30 kg
Acceleration (v) = 1.07 m/s²

So, the acceleration of the particle is $\boxed{1.07 \text{ m/s}^2}$ .
